      "text": "To find the average number of rounds played by each golfer, we need to determine the total number of rounds played and the total number of golfers.\n\nFrom the chart, we see that:\n- 1 golfer played 1 round.\n- 2 golfers played 2 rounds.\n- 2 golfers played 3 rounds.\n- 3 golfers played 4 rounds.\n- 5 golfers played 5 rounds.\n\nFirst, calculate the total number of rounds played:\n\\[\n1 \\text{ round} \\times 1 \\text{ golfer} + 2 \\text{ rounds} \\times 2 \\text{ golfers} + 3 \\text{ rounds} \\times 2 \\text{ golfers} + 4 \\text{ rounds} \\times 3 \\text{ golfers} + 5 \\text{ rounds} \\times 5 \\text{ golfers}\n\\]\n\\[\n= 1 \\times 1 + 2 \\times 2 + 3 \\times 2 + 4 \\times 3 + 5 \\times 5\n\\]\n\\[\n= 1 + 4 + 6 + 12 + 25\n\\]\n\\[\n= 48 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate the total number of golfers:\n\\[\n1 \\text{ golfer} + 2 \\text{ golfers} + 2 \\text{ golfers} + 3 \\text{ golfers} + 5 \\text{ golfers}\n\\]\n\\[\n= 1 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 5\n\\]\n\\[\n= 13 \\text{ golfers}\n\\]\n\nNow, calculate the average number of rounds played by each golfer:\n\\[\n\\text{Average} = \\frac{\\text{Total rounds}}{\\text{Total golfers}} = \\frac{48}{13}\n\\]\n\nTo convert this fraction to a decimal:\n\\[\n\\frac{48}{13} \\approx 3.6923\n\\]\n\nRounding 3.6923 to the nearest whole number gives us:\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]",
