      "text": "To find the average number of rounds played by each golfer, we first need to determine the total number of rounds played by all the golfers and then divide that total by the number of golfers.\n\nFrom the chart, we can see that:\n- 5 golfers played 1 round\n- 2 golfers played 2 rounds\n- 2 golfers played 3 rounds\n- 3 golfers played 4 rounds\n- 5 golfers played 5 rounds\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of rounds played:\n\\[\n5 \\text{ golfers} \\times 1 \\text{ round/golfer} = 5 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\text{ golfers} \\times 2 \\text{ rounds/golfer} = 4 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\text{ golfers} \\times 3 \\text{ rounds/golfer} = 6 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\\[\n3 \\text{ golfers} \\times 4 \\text{ rounds/golfer} = 12 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\\[\n5 \\text{ golfers} \\times 5 \\text{ rounds/golfer} = 25 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\nAdding these together gives the total number of rounds played:\n\\[\n5 + 4 + 6 + 12 + 25 = 52 \\text{ rounds}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the total number of golfers by summing up all the golfers:\n\\[\n5 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 5 = 17 \\text{ golfers}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we find the average number of rounds played by each golfer by dividing the total number of rounds by the total number of golfers:\n\\[\n\\frac{52 \\text{ rounds}}{17 \\text{ golfers}} \\approx 3.0588\n\\]\n\nRounding 3.0588 to the nearest whole number gives us:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]",
